# Kengrean — Korean Through Stories

- Start all responses with '🤖: '

# File Organization
- `index.html` is the shell; it loads plain `<script>` files in order (no build step, no frameworks).
- `js/core.js`: KG registry, helpers (`KG.h`, `KG.fill`, `KG.util`) and saved progress (`KG.store`).
- `js/hangul.js` (syllable blocks, particles, romanization), `js/audio.js` (clips + speech fallback), `js/ui.js` (shared UI), `js/learn.js` (path, unit, story player, letters, words, patterns), `js/games.js` (quiz modes, session runner, arcade games, practice hub), `js/app.js` (router, library, settings, boot).
- Course content lives in `content/*.js` and follows `content/SCHEMA.md`. Never hard-code lesson content in `js/`.
- Generated assets: `audio/*.mp3` + `audio/manifest.js`, `img/stories/*.webp`. Do not edit by hand.

# Code Style
- camelCase names, 4-space indentation, single quotes.
- Build DOM with `KG.h('tag.class', props, ...children)`; replace children with `KG.fill(node, ...)`.
- All saved state goes through `KG.store` (localStorage key `kengrean.v2`).
- Group related functions under `// =====` section comments.

# Content Rules
- Standard Seoul Korean, polite 해요체; check particles against batchim and every conjugation.
- Each story scene needs an `art` description that makes the meaning visible (comprehensible input); never ask for text in images.
- Run `node tools/validate_content.mjs` after editing content.

# Audio & Images
- After changing Korean text: `node tools/extract_tts.mjs --prune` then `python tools/gen_audio.py` (Edge neural voices via `edge-tts`, free).
- Each cast member has a fixed voice in `content/cast.js`; keep `voiceKey` in `js/audio.js` and `tools/extract_tts.mjs` identical.
- New story scenes: `node tools/gen_images.mjs scenes <unit-id>` (uses `OPENAI_API_KEY`; never print or commit the key). The cast sheet `img/ref/cast-sheet.png` keeps characters consistent.

# Testing
- Serve the folder (e.g. `python -m http.server 8765`) and check desktop and a 375px phone width.
- Check the story player, a full lesson, and each arcade game after changes to `js/`.
